<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Styria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Steiermark</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Styria (Steiermark) is a mountainous region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graz">Graz</a>. It takes its name from the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steyr">Steyr</a>, seat of the Otakar margraves who ruled it from 1056. It became a duchy in 1180 and passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1282, remaining one of their core lands. Its southern part, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-styria">Lower Styria</a>, went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> in 1919 and now belongs to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/styria.jpg" alt="Styria" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Made by Jon Harald Søby from File:Steiermark Landesfarben.PNG, colours and ratio adjusted by Mevsfotw. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Styria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
